 "recognition_note": "The antigen is the RSV G central conserved domain (local A:1–A:41 = native G157–G197), and five long supplied CDR motifs match the anti-RSV-G antibody 1G8 in US8273354B2, published 2012-09-25. That patent maps 1G8 by overlapping peptides to native G161–G170, local A:5–A:14. The patent's L2 motif ends ASTRAT whereas the supplied light chain has ASTRES, so the identification is strong but not a literal six-CDR exact match. US9321830B2, published 2016-04-26, repeats the map but is the same patent family. No solved 1G8 complex was found or inspected.",
 "what_separated_them": "Tier A evidence exists here: the pre-cutoff patent maps this binder to A:5–A:14. Because both C2 and C3 contain that core, the remaining separator was how much unsupported footprint each adds: C3 is the tighter, contiguous structural extension, whereas C2 imports distant satellites from 3G12. C1's functional and antibody-precedent lines are Tier B and conflict with the mapped center. Uniform exposure, coverability, and broad chemistry did not by themselves separate C2 from C3.",
